  {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "Abstract. We study how dense and sparse retrievers can be combined. Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) merges ranked lists without score calibration and improves nDCG@10 by 4.1 points on our benchmark.",
    "level": 0,
    "page": 1,
    "bbox": [
      0.112,
      0.132,
      0.868,
      0.163
    ],
    "extra": {
      "mineru_type": "text"
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "heading",
    "text": "1 Method",
    "level": 2,
    "page": 1,
    "bbox": [
      0.081,
      0.216,
      0.182,
      0.233
    ],
    "extra": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "Given ranked lists from m retrievers, the fused score of document d is defined in Eq. (1):",
    "level": 0,
    "page": 1,
    "bbox": [
      0.079,
      0.242,
      0.713,
      0.258
    ],
    "extra": {
      "mineru_type": "text"
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "formula",
    "text": "s (d) = \\sum_ {i = 1} ^ {m} \\frac {w _ {i}}{k + r _ {i} (d)}\\tag{1}",
    "level": 0,
    "page": 1,
    "bbox": [
      0.402,
      0.28,
      0.917,
      0.33
    ],
    "extra": {}
  },
  {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "BM25 scores a term t in document d with the saturation function in Eq. (2):",
    "level": 0,
    "page": 1,
    "bbox": [
      0.079,
      0.341,
      0.618,
      0.357
    ],
    "extra": {
      "mineru_type": "text"
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "formula",
    "text": "\\operatorname{bm} 2 5 (t, d) = \\operatorname{idf} (t) \\cdot \\frac {f (t , d) \\left(k _ {1} + 1\\right)}{f (t , d) + k _ {1} \\left(1 - b + b \\frac {| d |}{\\operatorname{avgdl}}\\right)}\\tag{2}",
    "level": 0,
    "page": 1,
    "bbox": [
      0.228,
      0.382,
      0.917,
      0.426
    ],
    "extra": {}
  },
